{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe MCP endpoint's `401` challenge advertises a protected-resource metadata URL that does not\nexist at the edge.\n\n    www-authenticate: Bearer error=\"invalid_token\", ...\n      resource_metadata=\"https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"\n\n    GET https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp -> 404\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nRFC 9728 metadata discovery is how an OAuth-capable client learns where to authenticate. A\nclient that follows the advertised URL gets a 404 and cannot discover the resource server.\n\nToday's clients use STATIC bearer PATs and do not consult it, so nothing is currently broken in\npractice — which is why this is P3 rather than higher. It matters if/when OAuth clients are\nenabled, and an advertised-but-missing URL is misleading regardless.\n\n## Pre-existing, not caused by the HTTPS-downgrade fix\n\nConfirmed against the pre-change backup of `/etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf`: there is no such\nlocation block BEFORE or AFTER that deploy. The nginx config has never served the path.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed, see the RCA comment)\n\nThe application already serves the document — probed from the box, the app direct on\n`127.0.0.1:8091` returns `200` for `/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` while the edge\nreturns `404`. `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` declares only `location = /mcp/`, `location =\n/mcp`, the prefix `location /mcp`, and `location /.well-known/acme-challenge/`. The advertised\npath matches none of them, so it falls through to `location /` -> `proxy_pass\nhttp://127.0.0.1:8080` (Gerrit), which 404s.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd ONE exact-match nginx location for the advertised path to the port-443 server block in\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template`, proxying to the existing named upstream with NO URI path on\n`proxy_pass`, so the request URI reaches the app verbatim — exactly the path the app already\nanswers with 200.\n\nWhy this approach fits: the defect is purely a missing edge route (the app half already works),\nso the narrowest correct fix is one routing rule and nothing else. `location =` (exact match)\nis used rather than a prefix so it cannot widen `/.well-known/` beyond this single document and\ncannot shadow the existing `location /.well-known/acme-challenge/` used by certbot. The\nupstream is named — `upstream rebar_mcp { include /etc/nginx/mcp-upstream*.conf; }` at\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:56-58` — so the new block reuses `proxy_pass\nhttp://rebar_mcp;` and inherits the blue-green atomic flip instead of hardcoding a port. The\nblock carries the same forwarded headers and `proxy_redirect` http->https upgrade rules the\nexisting MCP blocks carry (`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:157,178,195`), because an\nexact-match location inherits nothing from the prefix location.\n\nThis is a correctness/standards fix, not an outage fix. It deliberately does NOT touch the\nauthentication path, the 401 challenge text, or `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` — new `location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp`\n  in the 443 server block, before `location /`.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` — regression test, alongside the existing nginx\n  contract tests (`test_nginx_mcp_location_proxies_to_the_named_upstream` at line 156 and\n  `test_nginx_serves_the_documented_mcp_slash_url_without_redirecting` at line 834).\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: the RENDERED config (the template passed through `envsubst '${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}'`,\n  the exact substitution documented at `infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template:5-12`) contains an\n  exact-match `location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` whose body is\n  `proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp;` with no URI path, so the advertised URI is preserved.\n- Edge: the same rendered output still contains `location /.well-known/acme-challenge/` with\n  its `root /var/www/certbot;`, proving the new exact-match block does not shadow ACME\n  issuance/renewal; and the rendered text contains no unsubstituted `${` sequence, proving the\n  new block introduced nothing envsubst would eat.\n- Mutation check: deleting the new location block from the template must turn the new test RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The edge routes the advertised metadata URL to the MCP app instead of falling through to\n      Gerrit: the rendered nginx config contains an exact-match\n      `location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp` proxying to `http://rebar_mcp`\n      with no URI path; verified by a new test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` that\n      renders the template and asserts the block, and that fails when the block is removed.\n- [ ] A check fails if the advertised `resource_metadata` URL is not routable at the edge:\n      the same new test is the in-session observable proxy — it renders the template and fails\n      if no location matches the advertised path (live fetchability is only observable after a\n      deploy, which is out of scope for this ticket).\n- [ ] The new block does not regress ACME or MCP routing: the rendered config still carries\n      `location /.well-known/acme-challenge/` with `root /var/www/certbot;`, and the existing\n      nginx tests in `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` still pass.\n- [ ] Gates are green: `make lint`, `make typecheck`,\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py`, and\n      `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` all exit 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787946156385275391,"uuid":"0ab1fdc8-40f7-4fff-a482-598ac59492ca"}